  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Introducing Improved Climate Insurance Products to Smallholder Coffee Farmers</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The effects of climate change expose hundreds of millions of smallholder farmers to droughts and other severe weather that puts their livelihoods at risk. Insurance can help protect farmers against losses but is usually unavailable or too expensive for smallholders to purchase. With access to insurance, farmers are expected to have higher risk tolerance and be more likely to invest in farm inputs that can increase their productivity. The implementing partner offers seasonal climate insurance to protect smallholder farmers. To make insurance more affordable while still commercially viable, the implementing partner bases insurance payouts on predetermined, explicit conditions, called index insurance. Index insurance lowers claim processing costs and increases trust with smallholder farmers. The implementing partner also provides weather-prompted information and advice to farmers via mobile phones, such as guidance for dealing with unexpected weather patterns, to enable farmers to manage more climate risks independently. Satellite data and other digital tools help keep risk profile assessments and claim processing costs low as well. The implementing partner will introduce its suite of digital products through its Climate Smart CoffeeTM program, pilot them with 1,000 coffee farmers in Kenya, and conduct an impact study to understand whether coffee farmers incomes or investments have increased after obtaining this insurance. The implementing partner aims to reduce climate protection costs and increase on-farm investment, enabling smallholder farmers to improve their climate resilience and incomes.</narrative>
  </description>
